{"id": 3, "ts": 1779254767.9278142, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "agent_1", "message": "I provisionally favor **Candidate\u202fD** for the long\u2011distance pilot role.\n**Key evidence supporting D:** strong ability to respond to unexpected events, excellent concentration, outstanding problem\u2011solving, and a serious sense of responsibility \u2013 all critical for safe, extended flights where conditions can change rapidly.\n**Weaknesses:** regarded as arrogant and has relatively weak leadership skills, which could affect crew morale and coordination.\n**Major alternatives:**\n- **Candidate\u202fC** is 100\u202f% reliable, makes quick correct decisions and creates a positive crew atmosphere, but struggles with communication, is egocentric, and shows little interest in further professional development.\n- **Candidate\u202fB** is very conscientious, handles stress well, and has strong technical (weather, computer) skills, yet can be grumpy and uncooperative, raising concerns for teamwork.\n- **Candidate\u202fA** shows excellent anticipation, complex\u2011connection insight, spatial vision, and good leadership, but is sometimes unorganized and poorly receives criticism, which may impact reliability and safety.\n**Main trade\u2011off:** D\u2019s operational competence versus his weaker leadership and potential crew friction; the alternatives each have a different critical shortfall (communication for C, cooperation for B, organization for A).\n**Remaining uncertainty:** How severe D\u2019s arrogance and leadership gaps are in practice, and whether they would materially impair crew cooperation on long flights. Additional insight into D\u2019s crew interaction style would be decisive.\nMETADATA_JSON:\n{\"agent\": \"agent_1\", \"vote\": \"Candidate D\"}", "thoughts": "We need to produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON. We have to evaluate candidates based on given attributes. We have only our own info? The prompt says each agent holds a di