fficulty communicating ideas\", \"C is regarded as egocentric\", \"C is not very willing to further his education\", \"C keeps calm in a crisis\", \"C understands complicated technology\". So strengths: quick correct decisions, calm in crisis, technical understanding. Weaknesses: communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education.\n\nCandidate D: strengths: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously. Weaknesses: regarded as a know-it-all, has a hot temper. Also \"arrogant\"? Not in list but \"know-it-all\" similar. So weaknesses: hot temper, know-it-all (could affect teamwork).\n\nNow evaluate criteria:\n\nReliability/responsibility: D takes responsibility seriously. B very conscientious. C quick decisions maybe reliable. A leadership but show-off.\n\nTechnical/cognitive competence: A spatial vision, complex connections. B weather assessment, computer skills. C technology understanding, quick decisions. D problem solving, concentration.\n\nCalmness/judgment under pressure: B handles stress well. C keeps calm in crisis. D responds to unexpected events adequately. A anticipate dangerous situations.\n\nDecision-making: C quick correct decisions. D problem solving. A sees complex connections.\n\nTeamwork/communication: A leadership but show-off, not open to new ideas. B nasty remarks, uncooperative. C difficulty communicating, egocentric. D hot temper, know-it-all.\n\nProfessional development: C not willing to further education. Others not mentioned.\n\nThus trade-offs: D strong on responsibility, problem solving, concentration, but teamwork issues (hot temper, know-it-all). B strong on conscientiousness, stress handling, technical, but memory issues and nasty remarks. C strong on decision-making, calmness, technical, but communication and egocentric. A strong on anticipation, leadership, spatial vision, but show-off, not open to new ideas.\n\nLong-distance flights require crew coordination over long periods, so teamwork and communication are crucial. Also ability to handle unexpected events and maintain concentration. D's hot temper could be problematic over long flights. B's nasty remarks also problematic. C's communication difficulty also problematic. A's show-off and rigidity could affect crew morale.\n\nWhich candidate balances best? Possibly D: responsibility, problem solving, concentration, handling unexpected events are critical. Teamwork issues may be mitigated by leadership? But leadership is weak. A has leadership but show-off and rigidity.\n\nMaybe B: conscientiousness, stress handling, weather assessment (important for long flights), computer skills. But nasty remarks could degrade crew.\n\nC: quick decisions, calm, technical, but communication issues.\n\nGiven the importance of crew cohesion over long flights, perhaps candidate with best teamwork is none? But we have limited info. A's leadership may help crew despite show-off? Show-off could be minor. Not open to new ideas could hinder adaptability.\n\nWe need to state provisional preference with confidence level. I think D still seems strongest operationally, but teamwork concerns. I might be undecided, leaning to D but need more info on how his hot temper manifests and teamwork. So vote D with moderate confidence, note uncertainty about crew interaction.\n\nThus produce public message."}
